message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "literature-extraction-student: A Claude skill for learning data extraction in systematic reviews"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24388715
repository-code: "https://github.com/rnrnrnn1234/literature-extraction-student"
abstract: >-
  A Claude skill for students learning data extraction for systematic reviews.
  For each paper the student classifies the study design, chooses extraction items
  and enters values first; Claude extracts independently and explains only the
  discrepancies (role of the item, evidence sentence in the paper, why that value,
  common pitfalls). Results are saved to an Excel workbook with the extraction table,
  the student–Claude comparison record and item definitions.
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - data extraction
  - nursing education
  - research methodology
  - Claude skill
